    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 5th with a primary objective of securing stolen base upside, though our strongest offensive output tonight is anchored by high-floor anchors. **Trea Turner** (77.31) and **Kyle Schwarber** (73.41) are our premier starts, both benefiting from a favorable matchup against Severino. **Trea Turner** remains our most essential catalyst, leveraging his dynamic platoon profile and leadoff positioning to exploit a 4.59 xERA starter. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces the stiffest test of the night against the elite arm of Ohtani (2.81 xERA), his xwOBA of 0.428 mandates his inclusion; despite the difficult matchup, his individual profile effectively mitigates the risk of a sub-par performance.\n\nOur secondary tier focuses heavily on exploiting platoon and speed advantages. **Dillon Dingler** (63.89) and **Chase Meidroth** (62.45) receive significant boosts from favorable platoon splits against left-handed pitching, with **Chase Meidroth**\u2019s leadoff placement providing a 10% efficiency bump. While **Junior Caminero** (58.25) landed just below the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold due to the challenge of facing Gausman, he remains in the UTIL spot as our best available option, as depth options like **Hyeseong Kim** and **Colt Keith** are confirmed out of the lineup. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (55.42) provides a specific strategic utility; even with a challenging platoon profile, his 87% stolen base delivery rating against the opposing starter makes him a vital, albeit high-variance, asset in our pursuit of category scarcity. \n\nThe decision to bench the remaining roster was driven by availability and situational risk. **Carson Benge** was an immediate exclusion due to a confirmed rainout, ensuring we avoid a zero in the box score. Aside from the IL-stashed **Christian Yelich**, our decision-making process was relatively straightforward today given the clear stratification in the ATC projections. We are proceeding with this configuration to prioritize the combination of **Trea Turner**\u2019s speed, **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s power, and the platoon-heavy approach at the top of the order to navigate a slate featuring several elite arms.",
